And he is trying very hard to explain that he had a whole bit with a chainsaw that he hasn't been able to do.
他非常努力地解释说他原本准备了一个电锯的桥段，但一直没机会表演。

1545
01:02:13.160 --> 01:02:13.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1546
01:02:13.780 --> 01:02:15.360
And Karen's like, you know what?
凯伦说，你知道吗？

1547
01:02:15.480 --> 01:02:18.880
Why don't you just put it all in an email and I'll send it to my team?
你为什么不把它写在邮件里，我发给我的团队看？

1548
01:02:18.880 --> 01:02:21.900
And he's like, I can't put a chainsaw in an email, Karen.
他说，凯伦，我没法把电锯放进邮件里。

1549
01:02:22.160 --> 01:02:22.860
I can't do it.
我做不到。

1550
01:02:23.540 --> 01:02:27.060
This is when Pam and Karen are going to have a little bonding moment.
接下来就是帕姆和凯伦建立感情的时刻了。

1551
01:02:27.280 --> 01:02:27.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1552
01:02:27.900 --> 01:02:29.140
It's so sweet.
太甜了。

1553
01:02:29.680 --> 01:02:31.180
Pam says, when are you due?
帕姆问，你预产期是什么时候？

1554
01:02:31.740 --> 01:02:34.000
And Karen says, I'm due in a month.
凯伦说，我下个月就要生了。

1555
01:02:34.720 --> 01:02:35.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1556
01:02:35.820 --> 01:02:38.220
Michael says, who did this to you?
迈克尔问，是谁把你搞成这样的？

1557
01:02:39.060 --> 01:02:40.560
Who did this to you, Karen?
是谁把你搞成这样的，凯伦？

1558
01:02:41.260 --> 01:02:42.440
She's like, my husband.
她说，是我丈夫。

1559
01:02:43.040 --> 01:02:44.360
He's a dermatologiSt.
他是个皮肤科医生。

1560
01:02:44.360 --> 01:02:45.460
We met at a bar.
我们在酒吧认识的。

1561
01:02:45.860 --> 01:02:47.860
And then they have all these cute photos.
然后他们还有好多可爱的照片。

1562
01:02:47.860 --> 01:02:50.120
They have one where they're like dressed like hot dogs.
有一张是他们打扮成热狗的样子。

1563
01:02:50.880 --> 01:02:52.780
Yes, a hot dog and a hamburger.
没错，一个热狗和一个汉堡包。

1564
01:02:53.300 --> 01:02:54.520
It's very cute.
非常可爱。

1565
01:02:54.840 --> 01:02:57.620
We had a lot of fan questions about this.
我们收到了很多粉丝关于这个问题的提问。

1566
01:02:58.140 --> 01:03:01.000
Everyone wants to know, who is the man in the photo?
大家都想知道，照片里的男人是谁？

1567
01:03:01.000 --> 01:03:05.440
Who is Dan, the dermatologist, who is married to Karen?
那个和凯伦结婚的皮肤科医生丹是谁？

1568
01:03:06.040 --> 01:03:09.200
Well, it was played by writer Dan Gore.
嗯，他是编剧丹·戈尔演的。

1569
01:03:09.560 --> 01:03:09.940
Yeah.
没错。

1570
01:03:10.400 --> 01:03:12.880
He was a writer on Parks and Recreation.
他曾是《公园与游憩》的编剧。

1571
01:03:12.880 --> 01:03:17.240
Yes, and he had been working with Mike Schur and Greg Daniels as they developed that show.
是的，他在迈克·舒尔和格雷格·丹尼尔斯开发那部剧时就和他们一起工作了。

1572
01:03:17.420 --> 01:03:21.460
And we had seen him a few times on set and in the writer's room meeting with those guys.
我们曾在片场和编剧室见过他几次，他和那些人开会。

1573
01:03:21.960 --> 01:03:25.900
And he came to set one day when we were shooting on the stages,
有一天我们在摄影棚拍摄时，他来到了片场，

1574
01:03:25.900 --> 01:03:28.420
and he and Rashida dressed up in all these different outfits,
他和拉什达换上了各种不同的服装，

1575
01:03:28.420 --> 01:03:30.300
and they went around and took pictures.
到处拍照。

1576
01:03:32.380 --> 01:03:33.460
It was amazing.
太棒了。

1577
01:03:33.600 --> 01:03:34.220
It was amazing.
太棒了。

1578
01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:38.440
Well, you know, now Karen is going to ask about Jim.
嗯，你知道，现在凯伦要问起吉姆了。

1579
01:03:39.120 --> 01:03:39.560
Yes.
是的。

1580
01:03:39.560 --> 01:03:44.280
It's a little bit of tension, but Pam says we're engaged.
气氛有点紧张，但帕姆说我们订婚了。

1581
01:03:44.560 --> 01:03:47.800
And Karen is just earnestly happy for them.
而凯伦是真心为他们感到高兴。

1582
01:03:48.080 --> 01:03:48.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1583
01:03:48.720 --> 01:03:50.000
Rashida really sold it.
拉什达演得真好。

1584
01:03:50.120 --> 01:03:52.440
Because I think as an audience, you're like, oh, what's that?
因为我觉得作为观众，你会想，哦，那是什么情况？

1585
01:03:52.520 --> 01:03:55.180
And she's like, she has so moved on.
而她表现得，她已经彻底走出来了。

1586
01:03:55.340 --> 01:03:56.480
She has a whole life.
她有了全新的生活。

1587
01:03:56.540 --> 01:03:57.580
She's happy.
她很幸福。

1588
01:03:57.580 --> 01:04:00.160
And it gives Pam closure.
这让帕姆释怀了。

1589
01:04:00.620 --> 01:04:01.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1590
01:04:01.840 --> 01:04:09.260
I don't know about you, Ange, but I am happy if someone I have broken up with
安吉，我不知道你怎么想，但我如果和某人分手了，

1591
01:04:09.920 --> 01:04:14.640
finds, like, a new relationship with someone else and they're in love.
对方找到了新恋情并且坠入爱河，我会很高兴。

1592
01:04:15.200 --> 01:04:17.620
Because I'm like, yeah, that's why we broke up.
因为我会想，是啊，这就是我们分手的原因。

1593
01:04:17.680 --> 01:04:20.600
Because we weren't a match, and then you found your match.
因为我们不合适，然后你找到了你的真命天子。

1594
01:04:20.720 --> 01:04:23.180
I don't have a lot of hard feelings about stuff.
我对这些事没什么怨恨。

1595
01:04:23.320 --> 01:04:26.080
And I've had some messy breakups, you know?
虽然我也经历过一些糟糕的分手，你知道吗？

1596
01:04:26.080 --> 01:04:28.200
And even still, I don't know.
即便如此，我不知道。

1597
01:04:28.380 --> 01:04:30.780
I just, I think I am more Karen on this one.
我只是觉得，在这件事上我更像凯伦。

1598
01:04:30.860 --> 01:04:31.620
I'm like, well, great.
我会觉得，太好了。

1599
01:04:31.660 --> 01:04:35.220
I'm glad that worked out because, you know, good.
我很高兴事情能这样解决，因为，你知道，挺好的。

1600
01:04:35.460 --> 01:04:35.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1601
01:04:36.100 --> 01:04:40.120
It wasn't meant to be for me and Jim, but it's for you and Jim.
我和吉姆注定无缘，但你和吉姆却很合适。

1602
01:04:40.280 --> 01:04:40.560
Right.
没错。

1603
01:04:41.240 --> 01:04:42.960
No, I think life is short.
不，我觉得人生苦短。

1604
01:04:43.160 --> 01:04:45.940
My grandmother used to always say, every pot has its lid.
我奶奶常说，锅碗瓢盆各有配。

1605
01:04:46.140 --> 01:04:46.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1606
01:04:46.680 --> 01:04:48.520
